+# Design
+
+## Context
+
+The repository has no source yet: a TypeScript ESM package, tests run with `node --test`, no runtime dependencies. Later features will import this function, so it lives in its own module and is re-exported from `src/index.ts`.
+
+## Goals / Non-Goals
+
+**Goals:**
+- Follow RFC 6901 strictly, so that every invalid pointer is rejected rather than leniently interpreted.
+
+**Non-Goals:**
+- URI fragment form (`#/a%20b`), setting or removing values, and relative JSON pointers.
+
+## Decisions
+
+- **Throw `Error` for both failure kinds.** The request only asks for an error; a single `Error` subclass is not needed now. Messages state the reason and the token. Alternative: distinct error classes. Deferred until a consumer needs to tell them apart.
+- **Split on `/`, then unescape each token with `~1` → `/` first, then `~0` → `~`.** This order is required by the RFC so `~01` yields `~1`. Validate with a pattern rejecting `~` not followed by `0`/`1` before unescaping.
+- **Member lookup uses own-property checks** (`Object.hasOwn`), so `__proto__`, `constructor` and array `length` never resolve. This also avoids returning prototype internals to callers.
+- **Array index must match `^(0|[1-9][0-9]*)$` and be below the length.** `-` therefore fails naturally as it is not an index.
+- **Values are distinguished by `Array.isArray` and `typeof === "object" && !== null`**; any other value cannot be descended into.
+- **Compile with `tsc`-free tooling?** Node cannot run `.ts` directly on all versions; the implementation must pick a way to run tests on TypeScript (see tasks).
+
+## Risks / Trade-offs
+
+- [Test runner and TypeScript] `node --test` may not execute `.ts` files depending on the Node version → check the Node version first; use type stripping if available, otherwise add a minimal dev-only build step, without adding runtime dependencies.
