@@ -0,0 +1,23 @@
+## Why
+
+Our services need one standard way to refer to a value inside a JSON document. RFC 6901 (JSON Pointer) is that standard, and several upcoming features will build on it.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Add `resolvePointer(document, pointer)`, exported from `src/index.ts`, which returns the value a JSON Pointer refers to.
+- It throws when the pointer is not syntactically valid, or when it does not resolve to a value of the document.
+- Only the string representation of RFC 6901 section 5 is covered. The URI fragment representation (section 6) is out of scope.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+- `json-pointer`: parsing and evaluating RFC 6901 JSON Pointers against a JSON document.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+None.
+
+## Impact
+
+- New code in `src/` (the project has no source yet) and tests run by `node --test`.
+- Public API of the library gains one export. No dependencies added.
